@startuml Parallel Pipeline Data Flow Diagram

/'
    Parallel Pipeline Data Flow Diagram
    ===================================

    This diagram shows the complete data flow architecture of the parallel pipeline,
    illustrating how data moves through the system from input to output.

    Data Flow Patterns:
    - Ingestion: Raw data acquisition and validation
    - Processing: Data transformation and business logic
    - Streaming: Inter-task data communication
    - Output: Result delivery and persistence

    Flow Control:
    - Buffering: Capacity management and backpressure
    - Routing: Data distribution to appropriate processors
    - Synchronization: Ensuring data consistency across tasks

    Generated: 2026-01-05
    Version: 1.0
'/

title Parallel Pipeline Data Flow Architecture

' External data sources
database "External Data Sources" as ExtSources #LightBlue {
    [Message Queues] as MQ
    [Databases] as DB
    [REST APIs] as APIs
    [File Systems] as Files
    [Sensors/IoT] as Sensors
}

' Data ingestion layer
rectangle "Data Ingestion Layer" as Ingestion #LightYellow {
    rectangle "Input Adapters" as InputAdapters #LightCyan {
        [MQ Adapter] as MQAdapter
        [DB Adapter] as DBAdapter
        [REST Adapter] as RESTAdapter
        [File Adapter] as FileAdapter
        [Sensor Adapter] as SensorAdapter
    }

    rectangle "Data Validation" as Validation #LightCyan {
        [Schema Validator] as SchemaVal
        [Format Checker] as FormatCheck
        [Data Filter] as DataFilter
    }
}

' Processing layer
rectangle "Task Processing Layer" as Processing #LightGreen {
    rectangle "Task Instances" as TaskInstances #LightCyan {
        [Task 1\n(Data Producer)] as Task1
        [Task 2\n(Hybrid Task)] as Task2
        [Task 3\n(Data Consumer)] as Task3
        [Task N\n(Processor)] as TaskN
    }

    rectangle "Business Logic" as BusinessLogic #LightCyan {
        [Data Transformer] as Transformer
        [Aggregator] as Aggregator
        [Analyzer] as Analyzer
        [Decision Engine] as DecisionEngine
    }
}

' Data flow layer
rectangle "Data Flow Layer" as DataFlow #LightPink {
    rectangle "Stream Services" as StreamServices #LightCyan {
        [sensor_data stream] as SensorStream
        [processed_data stream] as ProcessedStream
        [alert_data stream] as AlertStream
        [result_data stream] as ResultStream
    }

    rectangle "Buffer Management" as Buffers #LightCyan {
        [FIFO Buffer] as FifoBuffer
        [Latest Buffer] as LatestBuffer
        [Sliding Window] as WindowBuffer
        [Priority Queue] as PriorityQueue
    }
}

' Output layer
rectangle "Data Output Layer" as Output #LightGray {
    rectangle "Output Adapters" as OutputAdapters #LightCyan {
        [Result Publisher] as Publisher
        [Data Exporter] as Exporter
        [Notification Service] as Notifier
        [Storage Writer] as StorageWriter
    }

    rectangle "Result Aggregation" as Aggregation #LightCyan {
        [Result Merger] as Merger
        [Summary Generator] as Summarizer
        [Report Builder] as Reporter
    }
}

' External data sinks
database "External Data Sinks" as ExtSinks #LightBlue {
    [Result Queues] as ResultMQ
    [Data Warehouse] as Warehouse
    [Monitoring DB] as MonitorDB
    [Log Storage] as LogStorage
    [Dashboard APIs] as Dashboards
}

' Main data flow connections
ExtSources --> InputAdapters : Raw Data Input
InputAdapters --> Validation : Structured Data
Validation --> TaskInstances : Validated Data
TaskInstances --> StreamServices : Inter-Task Data
StreamServices --> Buffers : Buffered Data
Buffers --> TaskInstances : Stream Data
TaskInstances --> OutputAdapters : Processed Results
OutputAdapters --> Aggregation : Formatted Results
Aggregation --> ExtSinks : Final Output

' Detailed internal flows
MQ --> MQAdapter : Queue Messages
DB --> DBAdapter : Database Records
APIs --> RESTAdapter : API Responses
Files --> FileAdapter : File Data
Sensors --> SensorAdapter : Sensor Readings

MQAdapter --> SchemaVal : Message Data
DBAdapter --> SchemaVal : Record Data
RESTAdapter --> SchemaVal : Response Data
FileAdapter --> SchemaVal : File Content
SensorAdapter --> SchemaVal : Sensor Data

SchemaVal --> FormatCheck : Schema-Validated Data
FormatCheck --> DataFilter : Format-Checked Data
DataFilter --> Task1 : Filtered Data

Task1 --> Transformer : Raw Task Data
Transformer --> SensorStream : Transformed Data
SensorStream --> FifoBuffer : Sensor Stream Data

FifoBuffer --> Task2 : Buffered Sensor Data
Task2 --> Analyzer : Sensor Analysis
Analyzer --> ProcessedStream : Analysis Results
ProcessedStream --> LatestBuffer : Latest Results

LatestBuffer --> Task3 : Latest Processed Data
Task3 --> DecisionEngine : Decision Input
DecisionEngine --> AlertStream : Decision Alerts
AlertStream --> PriorityQueue : Priority Alerts

PriorityQueue --> TaskN : Alert Data
TaskN --> Aggregator : Task Results
Aggregator --> Publisher : Aggregated Results

Publisher --> ResultMQ : Published Results
Exporter --> Warehouse : Exported Data
Notifier --> Dashboards : Notifications
StorageWriter --> MonitorDB : Monitoring Data
StorageWriter --> LogStorage : Log Data

' Control and metadata flows
Validation --> Buffers : Validation Metadata
Buffers --> Validation : Buffer Status
StreamServices --> TaskInstances : Data Availability
TaskInstances --> StreamServices : Data Consumption
Buffers --> StreamServices : Buffer Metrics

' Error and exception flows
Validation --> LogStorage : Validation Errors
TaskInstances --> LogStorage : Task Errors
StreamServices --> MonitorDB : Stream Errors
Buffers --> MonitorDB : Buffer Errors

note right of Ingestion : Data Ingestion:\n- Multi-protocol support\n- Data validation\n- Format normalization\n- Error filtering
note right of Processing : Task Processing:\n- Parallel execution\n- Business logic\n- Data transformation\n- Result aggregation
note right of DataFlow : Data Streaming:\n- Inter-task communication\n- Buffer management\n- Flow control\n- Data persistence
note right of Output : Data Output:\n- Multi-destination\n- Format adaptation\n- Result aggregation\n- Delivery guarantees

note as DataFlowNote
    **Data Flow Characteristics:**

    **Throughput**: High-volume data processing
    **Latency**: Low-latency requirements
    **Reliability**: Guaranteed delivery
    **Scalability**: Horizontal scaling support

    **Flow Control Mechanisms:**
    - Backpressure handling
    - Buffer overflow protection
    - Data rate limiting
    - Quality of service
end note

@enduml
